# Project Agents Context
# Last updated: 2026-09-28

## Project identity
- **CyberVault** — password manager with split-trust architecture: browser extension (MV3 service worker + popup), Core API (`src/infrastructure/api`, port 3010), Plus entitlement/challenge service (`plus/`, port 3011).
- Stack: TypeScript (strict), WebCrypto (PBKDF2 600k / HKDF), Jest + ts-jest, esbuild bundling (`scripts/build-extension.mjs`), optional SonarQube.

## Architecture
- `src/background/auditor.ts` — service worker: message router, all handlers, release/step-up/managed-release logic. Sole entry point for extension messaging.
- `src/background/message-types.ts` — the message contract; re-exported by `auditor.ts`. Content scripts and popup import from it so they cannot drift.
- `src/background/credential-release.ts` — release path (binding proof → guard → key derivation → decrypt). Fails closed on every failure path.
- `src/domain/services/autofill/` — origin canonicalization, opaque index, authoring, step-up binding rules, autofill guard.
- `src/infrastructure/crypto/master-key-manager.ts` — vault init/unlock, session key (`cybervault_session_key`, 15-min `SESSION_DURATION_MS`).
- `src/ui/popup/popup.ts|html` — popup UI; sends typed messages only.
- `src/ui/content-scripts/` — `autocomplete.js` (form fill), `managed-decrypt.js`, `inject.js`.
- Storage: `chrome.storage.session` holds `cybervault_vek` + `cybervault_session_key` + `cybervault_unlock_state`; `chrome.storage.local` holds `cybervault_cred_records` + `cybervault_cred_index` (ciphertext only).

## Current state
- Stage: **Pentest remediation H1–H7 complete + H6-Plus (Plus TLS fail-closed) applied + Plus API runtime T1–T5 applied (migration 005, `PostgresChallengeRepository`, `plus/api/main.ts`, `docker/Dockerfile.plus`, compose `plus` service) + `plus/admin` types T2–T7 (168 → 0 under its own tsconfig), awaiting orchestrator verification and commit.** Branch `fix/pentest-script-rdd`. Nothing committed by the agent. T6 (`.env` keys) and T7 (apply migration, boot the container, run the E2E capability cycle) remain the orchestrator's, as does **T1 of `plus-admin-types`** (exclude `plus/admin` from the root tsconfig include).
- SonarQube reports **0 open issues** for `cybervault`. A scanner token is generated per cycle via `api/user_tokens/generate` (e.g. `wu5-tls`) and passed as `-Dsonar.login=` (9.9 rejects `-Dsonar.token=`); a copy sits outside the repo at `/tmp/opencode/sonar.token`. No token is stored in the repo.
- SonarQube quality gate still ERROR, on metrics that are NOT open issues — measured against a re-scan of the reverted tree, so they predate the current change: `new_coverage` (jest `collectCoverageFrom` is `src/domain/**` only, so infrastructure changes can never count as covered), `new_duplicated_lines_density` ~3.3–3.4% > 3, `new_security_hotspots_reviewed` 0% (pre-existing hotspots, none in files touched).

## Objectives
1. ✅ WU-1 / WU-2 (prior sessions) — origin authority, managed-release contract fixes.
2. ✅ WU-3 — extension-side credential release path wired end to end (VEK persistence, authoring writer, step-up senders, popup senders, behavioural tests).
3. ✅ WU-4 — Plus-side capability gate: `/api/v1/capabilities/request` now decides before it signs, returns `challengeRequired`, reuses one challenge per binding; single signing key for issuer + challenge service.
4. ✅ Pentest H1–H7 — token type gate (H1), kebab-case CSP (H2), server-minted `secretRef` (H3), migration 003 + repository DDL mirror (H4), optional `expectedVersion` optimistic locking (H5), TLS fail-closed startup (H6), awaited session key (H7).
5. ✅ H6-Plus — `plus/api/server.ts` now refuses to start like Core does (production without `HTTPS_ENABLED` refuses; `HTTPS_ENABLED=true` with unreadable key/cert refuses in every environment; the plaintext fallback is gone). `PLUS_PUBLIC_KEY` pinning deliberately NOT added.
6. ✅ `plus/admin` types T2–T7 — 168 → 0 real errors under `plus/admin/tsconfig.json`, fixed by wiring the dead code (modals, footers, spinners) and mapping to the real `api.ts` shapes; no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`, no `_`-renames.
7. ⏳ Orchestrator verification + commit (explicitly out of agent scope).

## Project conventions
- English for all code, comments, tests, docs; no AI attribution in commits; conventional commits only.
- No new dependencies.
- Never weaken: ExactMatch guard, step-up binding re-check, JTI consumption. `origin.ts` is the sole origin authority.
- Regex-on-source assertions in tests constrain refactors — read them before editing `auditor.ts`.
- `plus/admin/`, Docker/compose files and the AITM pipeline are out of scope for remediation work units. `plus/` (API + domain) is in scope when the active work unit says so; WU-4 edited `plus/api/server.ts` and `plus/domain/services/challenge.ts` only.

## External dependencies
- Node 18+ (global `fetch`, WebCrypto). Playwright e2e requires Chrome (not installed here).
- SonarQube server + `sonarsource/sonar-scanner-cli` image ARE present locally (`docker compose -f docker-compose.sonarqube.yml up -d`, server on :9000, status UP) — but analysis needs a token and none is stored in the repo or `.env`.
- ESLint 8.57.1 is installed but **no ESLint config file exists anywhere**, so `npm run lint` fails for every file. Pre-existing; reported, not fixed.

## Points of attention
- **tsc baseline = 876 errors, all `plus/admin`** (866 TS17004 + 10 TS6142, every one "'--jsx' is not set"). `src/` and `plus/api/` are **0**. Was 803 before `odd/tasks/plus-admin-types.md`; it rose because T6 wired real JSX (spinners, footers, modals) into those pages — the root tsconfig cannot compile JSX at all, so more markup means more noise. The count goes to **0** only when **T1** excludes `plus/admin` from the root `"include": ["src/**/*", "plus/**/*"]`, which is still NOT applied (that line is the task owner's, not the sub-agent's). `npx tsc -p plus/admin/tsconfig.json --noEmit` = **0** (was 168). (807 until Plus T3, 809 before H7.)
- **jest baseline = 1036 passed / 0 failed, 17 skipped** (measured twice after the plus/admin types task). Was 1022 after row-mappers, 1002/1019 after H6-Plus, 989/1006 after H1–H7, 921/934 after WU-4.
- **`plus/admin` never built before**: `src/App.tsx` imported `./App.css`, a leftover Vite template import for a file that never existed → `vite build` failed. Import removed (all styles are in `src/index.css`, imported by `main.tsx`); `vite build` now succeeds. tsc never flagged it because `moduleResolution: "bundler"` leaves side-effect-only imports unchecked unless `noUncheckedSideEffectImports` is on.
- `jest.config.js` carries a narrow `diagnostics.exclude: ["**/plus/api/server.ts"]` so a test can import the real Plus route without ts-jest re-reporting that file's diagnostics. The 4 errors it was added for are gone (Plus T3); the carve-out was left in place — removing it is harmless but is not part of any current work unit. `tsc --noEmit` still covers the file. Deliberate, disclosed — do not widen it.
- Never write `password`/`totpSecret` inside a `chrome.storage.local.set(...)` body in `auditor.ts` — `tests/extension/sw-contract.test.ts` uses a non-greedy regex that can overrun to the next `)`.
- 15-min (`master-key-manager`) vs 30-min (`SESSION_WINDOW_MS`) session window discrepancy is reported, not silently unified.
- **Plus compiles with `@/…` path aliases but TS does not rewrite them at emit** — `dist/plus/**` used to require `@/shared/logger`, which plain Node cannot resolve, so the compiled Plus API could not boot at all. `plus/api/module-aliases.ts` (imported FIRST by `plus/api/main.ts`) hooks `Module._resolveFilename` and retries `@/…` against `dist/src`. Keep that import first.
- **Known defect NOT fixed (out of T1–T5):** the three existing Plus repos call `JSON.parse(row.metadata)` on a `jsonb` column that `pg` has already parsed, so any row with non-NULL `metadata` throws `SyntaxError` on read. Reachable from the T7 E2E cycle via `entitlementRepo.findByUserAndResource`.
- `.agents` and `.progress` are coordination state, not deliverables — but they ARE tracked (they are not in `.gitignore`), so edits to them show up in `git status`. Update them anyway; a stale baseline misleads the next agent more than diff noise does.
